    "research": {
      "notes": "**Coverage note:** I found no formal guidance, new litigation, customer-concentration news or insider buying for 2026-09-14 to 2026-10-14. The main events were the Rangers spin-off and ticket pricing.\n\n**1. Guidance / results**\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal found in the window. The company has not published formal numeric guidance in the sources I found. — n/a — no URL\n- The last results, fiscal Q4 and full year, were released before the window. Revenue was $278.7M, up 37%, driven by Knicks playoff revenue. — 2026-08-13 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001636519/000162828026056478/msgsportscorpex991forearni.htm\n- A StockTwits item says the quarter beat estimates on EPS and revenue. This is a secondary source. — 2026-08-13 — https://stocktwits.com/symbol/MSGS/news\n- The board approved the Rangers spin-off. It is expected to complete on 2026-10-26, with a record date of 2026-10-20. Each holder gets one MSG Rangers share for every two MSG Sports shares. — 2026-09-30 — https://investor.msgsports.com/press-releases/news-details/2026/MSG-Sports-Board-Approves-Spin-Off-of-Rangers-Business-From-Knicks-Business/default.aspx\n- After the spin, MSG Sports will be renamed MSG Knickerbockers Corp. (ticker \"MSGK\"). The Rangers company will trade as \"MSGR\". — 2026-09-30 — https://ng.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/msg-sports-board-clears-spinoff-of-rangers-from-knicks-business-2716791\n- The MSGS Spinco Form 10 registration became effective on 2026-10-09. — 2026-10-09 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002132873/000119312526419170/d122415d8k.htm\n- Yahoo lists the name change as effective 2026-10-27 and the next earnings date as an estimated 2026-10-30. — date unknown — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSGS/\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- I found no rating change or initiation dated inside the window.\n- A TipRanks headline says an analyst reiterated Buy with an unchanged $450 target, citing the spin narrowing the valuation gap. The firm and date are not shown, so I can't verify it. — date unknown — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/msgs\n- J.P. Morgan raised its target to $485 from $450 and kept Overweight. This is just before the window. — 2026-08-14 — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSGS/\n- Morgan Stanley upgraded to Overweight with a $450 target. This is before the window. — 2026-07-15 — https://finviz.com/stock?t=MSGS&ty=tr\n- Consensus targets differ by source:\n  - Yahoo shows an average of $480.67 and a high of $584. — date unknown — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSGS/\n  - Public.com shows an average of $468.20. — 2026-10-07 — https://public.com/stocks/msgs\n\n**3. Litigation / regulation**\n- No new lawsuit, investigation or fine against MSG Sports found in the window.\n- A proposed class action over a data breach, with up to 26M people affected, names MSG Entertainment (the venue owner) as the only defendant, not MSG Sports. It was filed before the window. — 2026-06-16 — https://frontofficesports.com/madison-square-garden-hit-with-class-action-after-apparent-data-breach/\n- The spin-off is intended to be tax-free. The 8-K coverage also cites NHL consent on future transfers. — 2026-09-30 — https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/MSGS-N/pressreleases/4917033/msg-sports-advances-rangers-spin-off-and-board-changes/\n- The spin-off will accelerate tax recognition of Rangers deferred revenue, about $20M if it had closed 2026-06-30. — 2026-09-30 — same Globe and Mail URL as above.\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- Nothing material found on customer concentration. Revenue comes from tickets, media rights, sponsorships and NBA league distributions. The sponsorship deals below are small.\n- Foot Locker became the Knicks' Official Athletic Footwear Retailer under a multi-year deal. — 2026-10-14 — https://www.stocktitan.net/news/MSGS/foot-locker-named-official-athletic-footwear-retailer-of-the-new-tq8bm2q0dm4k.html\n- Glaze Teriyaki was named a Madison Square Garden partner. This is listed on the company's news page. — 2026-09-30 — https://www.msgsports.com/company-news/\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- Bryan Warner (SVP, Head of Legal) had 291 and 417 shares vest on 2026-09-15 and had 254 withheld for tax at $393.27. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001636519/000119312526394317/ownership.xml\n- He then sold 628 shares on the open market at $393.77, leaving him with zero directly held shares. — 2026-09-16 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001636519/000119312526394317/ownership.xml\n- David Granville-Smith (EVP) had several vestings. He had 6,092 and 2,645 shares withheld for tax at $393.27. These are not open-market sales. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001636519/000119312526394328/ownership.xml\n- A further 2026-09-15 Form 4 shows vesting and tax withholding of 10,048 and 8,369 shares. The reporting owner isn't shown in the extract. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001636519/000119312526394314/ownership.xml\n- No insider purchases or 10b5-1 plan sales were found. Apart from Warner's sale, the 2026-09-15 filings are vesting and tax withholding, not clustered selling.\n- Jamaal Lesane moved from COO to EVP and Chief Legal Officer. Warner ceased to be an executive officer. — 2026-09-21 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001636519/000119312526397309/d152993d8k.htm\n\n**6. Product / competitive**\n- The Knicks paused single-game ticket sales after a pricing error. Some Oct. 20 opener seats were listed above $1,000. — 2026-09-17 — https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/knicks-pause-ticket-sales-error-171910005.html\n- MSG said it would roll back to last year's prices plus an average 12% increase, and refund buyers the difference. — 2026-09-17 — https://www.usnews.com/news/sports/articles/2026-09-17/knicks-pause-ticket-sales-after-error-caused-them-to-be-listed-at-prices-too-high\n- Board changes tied to the spin: five directors will resign from MSG Sports and join the MSG Rangers board. Irving Azoff and Isiah Thomas will be appointed to the MSG Sports board. — 2026-09-30 — https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/MSGS-N/pressreleases/4917033/msg-sports-advances-rangers-spin-off-and-board-changes/\n- Share price was about $405 after a 2% one-day drop, up about 5% over 30 days. — 2026-10-01 — https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-msgs/madison-square-garden-sports/news/madison-square-garden-sports-msgs-could-be-16-undervalued-fo\n- No competitor, share-shift or launch news found.",
